<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1 (Loss Sensitivity to Activation-Based Compression). ‣ 3.2 Activation-Aware Compression and Network Loss ‣ 3 Pareto-Guided Rank Selection ‣ Activation-Informed Pareto-Guided Low-Rank Compression for Efficient LLM/VLM" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a></h2>

<div id="A1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A1.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\|\cdot\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\cdot\|</annotation></semantics></math> be the operator (spectral) norm and <math id="A1.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\|\cdot\|_{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\cdot\|_{F}</annotation></semantics></math> the Frobenius norm.
For batch size <math id="A1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math>, let
<math id="A1.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbf{X}_{l}=[\boldsymbol{x}_{l}^{(1)}\,\cdots\,\boldsymbol{x}_{l}^{(B)}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>l</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.170em">⋯</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>l</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{X}_{l}=[\boldsymbol{x}_{l}^{(1)}\,\cdots\,\boldsymbol{x}_{l}^{(B)}]</annotation></semantics></math> and define:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx12" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\boldsymbol{z}_{l}^{(i)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>l</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\boldsymbol{z}_{l}^{(i)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbf{W}_{l}\boldsymbol{x}_{l}^{(i)}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>l</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbf{W}_{l}\boldsymbol{x}_{l}^{(i)},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbf{D}_{l}^{(i)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝐃</mi><mi>l</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbf{D}_{l}^{(i)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex16.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle:=\operatorname{diag}\!\big(\sigma^{\prime}(\boldsymbol{z}_{l}^{(i)})\big)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.736em;" width="1.736em"><mi>diag</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>l</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle:=\operatorname{diag}\!\big(\sigma^{\prime}(\boldsymbol{z}_{l}^{(i)})\big),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbf{J}_{l}^{(i)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝐉</mi><mi>l</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbf{J}_{l}^{(i)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex17.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle:=\mathbf{D}_{l}^{(i)}\mathbf{W}_{l}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐃</mi><mi>l</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle:=\mathbf{D}_{l}^{(i)}\mathbf{W}_{l}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Assume <math id="A1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\mathbf{X}_{1}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\mathbf{X}_{1}=0</annotation></semantics></math>. Using the first-order expansion (dropping second-order terms) for each sample <math id="A1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> we have:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx13" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Delta\boldsymbol{x}_{l+1}^{(i)}\;\approx\;\mathbf{D}_{l}^{(i)}\!\big(\mathbf{W}_{l}\Delta\boldsymbol{x}_{l}^{(i)}+\Delta\mathbf{W}_{l}\boldsymbol{x}_{l}^{(i)}\big)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐃</mi><mi>l</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>l</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>l</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Delta\boldsymbol{x}_{l+1}^{(i)}\;\approx\;\mathbf{D}_{l}^{(i)}\!\big(\mathbf{W}_{l}\Delta\boldsymbol{x}_{l}^{(i)}+\Delta\mathbf{W}_{l}\boldsymbol{x}_{l}^{(i)}\big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Assume <math id="A1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\mathbf{D}_{l}^{(i)}\|\leq c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐃</mi><mi>l</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\mathbf{D}_{l}^{(i)}\|\leq c</annotation></semantics></math>, then we have:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx14" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|\Delta\boldsymbol{x}_{l+1}^{(i)}\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|\Delta\boldsymbol{x}_{l+1}^{(i)}\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex19.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\|\mathbf{J}_{l}^{(i)}\|\,\|\Delta\boldsymbol{x}_{l}^{(i)}\|_{2}+c\,\|\Delta\mathbf{W}_{l}\boldsymbol{x}_{l}^{(i)}\|_{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐉</mi><mi>l</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>l</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>l</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\|\mathbf{J}_{l}^{(i)}\|\,\|\Delta\boldsymbol{x}_{l}^{(i)}\|_{2}+c\,\|\Delta\mathbf{W}_{l}\boldsymbol{x}_{l}^{(i)}\|_{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Stack columns and define:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx15" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbf{G}_{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐆</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbf{G}_{l}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex20.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle:=\big[\mathbf{J}_{l}^{(1)}\Delta\boldsymbol{x}_{l}^{(1)}\cdots\mathbf{J}_{l}^{(B)}\Delta\boldsymbol{x}_{l}^{(B)}\big]," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo lspace="0em">=</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐉</mi><mi>l</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>l</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐉</mi><mi>l</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>l</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle:=\big[\mathbf{J}_{l}^{(1)}\Delta\boldsymbol{x}_{l}^{(1)}\cdots\mathbf{J}_{l}^{(B)}\Delta\boldsymbol{x}_{l}^{(B)}\big],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbf{Q}_{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐐</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbf{Q}_{l}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex21.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle:=\big[\mathbf{D}_{l}^{(1)}\Delta\mathbf{W}_{l}\boldsymbol{x}_{l}^{(1)}\cdots\mathbf{D}_{l}^{(B)}\Delta\mathbf{W}_{l}\boldsymbol{x}_{l}^{(B)}\big]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo lspace="0em">=</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐃</mi><mi>l</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>l</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐃</mi><mi>l</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>l</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle:=\big[\mathbf{D}_{l}^{(1)}\Delta\mathbf{W}_{l}\boldsymbol{x}_{l}^{(1)}\cdots\mathbf{D}_{l}^{(B)}\Delta\mathbf{W}_{l}\boldsymbol{x}_{l}^{(B)}\big].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Then <math id="A1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\mathbf{X}_{l+1}\approx\mathbf{G}_{l}+\mathbf{Q}_{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐆</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝐐</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\mathbf{X}_{l+1}\approx\mathbf{G}_{l}+\mathbf{Q}_{l}</annotation></semantics></math> and:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx16" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|\mathbf{G}_{l}\|_{F}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝐆</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|\mathbf{G}_{l}\|_{F}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex22.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{i=1}^{B}\|\mathbf{J}_{l}^{(i)}\Delta\boldsymbol{x}_{l}^{(i)}\|_{2}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>B</mi></munderover></mstyle><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐉</mi><mi>l</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>l</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{i=1}^{B}\|\mathbf{J}_{l}^{(i)}\Delta\boldsymbol{x}_{l}^{(i)}\|_{2}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\;\Big(\sup_{i}\|\mathbf{J}_{l}^{(i)}\|^{2}\Big)\sum_{i=1}^{B}\|\Delta\boldsymbol{x}_{l}^{(i)}\|_{2}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mi>i</mi></munder><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐉</mi><mi>l</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>B</mi></munderover></mstyle><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>l</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\;\Big(\sup_{i}\|\mathbf{J}_{l}^{(i)}\|^{2}\Big)\sum_{i=1}^{B}\|\Delta\boldsymbol{x}_{l}^{(i)}\|_{2}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\Big(\sup_{i}\|\mathbf{J}_{l}^{(i)}\|\Big)^{2}\|\Delta\mathbf{X}_{l}\|_{F}^{2}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mi>i</mi></munder><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐉</mi><mi>l</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\Big(\sup_{i}\|\mathbf{J}_{l}^{(i)}\|\Big)^{2}\|\Delta\mathbf{X}_{l}\|_{F}^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex25"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|\mathbf{Q}_{l}\|_{F}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝐐</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|\mathbf{Q}_{l}\|_{F}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex25.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{i=1}^{B}\|\mathbf{D}_{l}^{(i)}\Delta\mathbf{W}_{l}\boldsymbol{x}_{l}^{(i)}\|_{2}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>B</mi></munderover></mstyle><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐃</mi><mi>l</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>l</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{i=1}^{B}\|\mathbf{D}_{l}^{(i)}\Delta\mathbf{W}_{l}\boldsymbol{x}_{l}^{(i)}\|_{2}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex26"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\;c^{2}\sum_{i=1}^{B}\|\Delta\mathbf{W}_{l}\boldsymbol{x}_{l}^{(i)}\|_{2}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><msup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>B</mi></munderover></mstyle><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>l</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\;c^{2}\sum_{i=1}^{B}\|\Delta\mathbf{W}_{l}\boldsymbol{x}_{l}^{(i)}\|_{2}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex27"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=c^{2}\|\Delta\mathbf{W}_{l}\mathbf{X}_{l}\|_{F}^{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=c^{2}\|\Delta\mathbf{W}_{l}\mathbf{X}_{l}\|_{F}^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">By triangle inequality in Frobenius norm we have:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx17" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex28"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|\Delta\mathbf{X}_{l+1}\|_{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|\Delta\mathbf{X}_{l+1}\|_{F}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex28.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\|\mathbf{G}_{l}\|_{F}+\|\mathbf{Q}_{l}\|_{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝐆</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝐐</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\|\mathbf{G}_{l}\|_{F}+\|\mathbf{Q}_{l}\|_{F}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex29"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\mathcal{K}_{l}\|\Delta\mathbf{X}_{l}\|_{F}+c\,\|\Delta\mathbf{W}_{l}\mathbf{X}_{l}\|_{F}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\mathcal{K}_{l}\|\Delta\mathbf{X}_{l}\|_{F}+c\,\|\Delta\mathbf{W}_{l}\mathbf{X}_{l}\|_{F},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A1.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{K}_{l}:=\sup_{i}\|\mathbf{J}_{l}^{(i)}\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">:=</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐉</mi><mi>l</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{K}_{l}:=\sup_{i}\|\mathbf{J}_{l}^{(i)}\|</annotation></semantics></math> and unrolling for <math id="A1.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l=1,\dots,L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l=1,\dots,L</annotation></semantics></math> we have:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx18" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex30"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|\Delta\mathbf{X}_{L+1}\|_{F}\;\leq\;\sum_{l=1}^{L}\Biggl(\prod_{m=l+1}^{L}\mathcal{K}_{m}\Biggr)c\,\|\Delta\mathbf{W}_{l}\mathbf{X}_{l}\|_{F}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mi>L</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|\Delta\mathbf{X}_{L+1}\|_{F}\;\leq\;\sum_{l=1}^{L}\Biggl(\prod_{m=l+1}^{L}\mathcal{K}_{m}\Biggr)c\,\|\Delta\mathbf{W}_{l}\mathbf{X}_{l}\|_{F}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">For a scalar loss <math id="A1.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}(\mathbf{Y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}(\mathbf{Y})</annotation></semantics></math> with
<math id="A1.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Y}=\mathbf{X}_{L+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐘</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Y}=\mathbf{X}_{L+1}</annotation></semantics></math>, first-order Taylor and Cauchy–Schwarz yield:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx19" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex31"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Delta\mathcal{L}\;" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Delta\mathcal{L}\;</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex31.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\approx\;\langle\nabla_{\mathbf{Y}}\mathcal{L},\,\Delta\mathbf{Y}\rangle_{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.558em">≈</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>𝐘</mi></msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐘</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\approx\;\langle\nabla_{\mathbf{Y}}\mathcal{L},\,\Delta\mathbf{Y}\rangle_{F}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex32"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Rightarrow|\Delta\mathcal{L}|\;\leq\;\|\nabla_{\mathbf{Y}}\mathcal{L}\|_{F}\,\|\Delta\mathbf{Y}\|_{F}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">⇒</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>𝐘</mi></msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐘</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Rightarrow|\Delta\mathcal{L}|\;\leq\;\|\nabla_{\mathbf{Y}}\mathcal{L}\|_{F}\,\|\Delta\mathbf{Y}\|_{F}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p8.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p8.2.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Proof of Proposition <a href="#Thmproposition1" title="Proposition 1 (Rank–𝜀 Allocation Equivalence). ‣ 3.3 Surrogate Pareto Frontier ‣ 3 Pareto-Guided Rank Selection ‣ Activation-Informed Pareto-Guided Low-Rank Compression for Efficient LLM/VLM" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a></h2>

<div id="A2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">(P <math id="A2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Rightarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">⇒</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Rightarrow</annotation></semantics></math> E)
Take any feasible ranks <math id="A2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{r_{l}\}_{l=1}^{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{r_{l}\}_{l=1}^{L}</annotation></semantics></math> for (P). Set <math id="A2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon_{l}:=e_{l}(r_{l})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon_{l}:=e_{l}(r_{l})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Since <math id="A2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{l}(\varepsilon_{l})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{l}(\varepsilon_{l})</annotation></semantics></math> is the <em id="A2.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">minimal</em> parameter count achieving error
<math id="A2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\leq\varepsilon_{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\leq\varepsilon_{l}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{l}(\varepsilon_{l})\leq P_{l}(r_{l})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{l}(\varepsilon_{l})\leq P_{l}(r_{l})</annotation></semantics></math> for each <math id="A2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>l</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l</annotation></semantics></math>.
Thus <math id="A2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{l}h_{l}(\varepsilon_{l})\leq\sum_{l}P_{l}(r_{l})\leq b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>l</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≤</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>l</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{l}h_{l}(\varepsilon_{l})\leq\sum_{l}P_{l}(r_{l})\leq b</annotation></semantics></math>, so
<math id="A2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\varepsilon_{l}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\varepsilon_{l}\}</annotation></semantics></math> is feasible for (E), and the (E) objective equals
<math id="A2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{l}\alpha_{l}\,\varepsilon_{l}=\sum_{l}\alpha_{l}\,e_{l}(r_{l})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>l</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>l</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{l}\alpha_{l}\,\varepsilon_{l}=\sum_{l}\alpha_{l}\,e_{l}(r_{l})</annotation></semantics></math>, the surrogate objective in (P).
Taking the infimum over feasible <math id="A2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{r_{l}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{r_{l}\}</annotation></semantics></math> gives <math id="A2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{OPT}_{\text{(E)}}\leq\mathrm{OPT}_{\text{(P)}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>OPT</mi><mtext>(E)</mtext></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>OPT</mi><mtext>(P)</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{OPT}_{\text{(E)}}\leq\mathrm{OPT}_{\text{(P)}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">(E <math id="A2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Rightarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">⇒</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Rightarrow</annotation></semantics></math> P)
Let <math id="A2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\varepsilon_{l}^{\star}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>ε</mi><mi>l</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\varepsilon_{l}^{\star}\}</annotation></semantics></math> be optimal for (E). For each <math id="A2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>l</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l</annotation></semantics></math>, pick
<math id="A2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{l}^{\star}\in\arg\min\{P_{l}(r):e_{l}(r)\leq\varepsilon_{l}^{\star}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>l</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msubsup><mi>ε</mi><mi>l</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{l}^{\star}\in\arg\min\{P_{l}(r):e_{l}(r)\leq\varepsilon_{l}^{\star}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, so that
<math id="A2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{l}(r_{l}^{\star})=h_{l}(\varepsilon_{l}^{\star})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>l</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>ε</mi><mi>l</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{l}(r_{l}^{\star})=h_{l}(\varepsilon_{l}^{\star})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{l}(r_{l}^{\star})\leq\varepsilon_{l}^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>l</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msubsup><mi>ε</mi><mi>l</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{l}(r_{l}^{\star})\leq\varepsilon_{l}^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then <math id="A2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{l}P_{l}(r_{l}^{\star})=\sum_{l}h_{l}(\varepsilon_{l}^{\star})\leq b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>l</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>l</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>l</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>ε</mi><mi>l</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{l}P_{l}(r_{l}^{\star})=\sum_{l}h_{l}(\varepsilon_{l}^{\star})\leq b</annotation></semantics></math>, so <math id="A2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{r_{l}^{\star}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>l</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{r_{l}^{\star}\}</annotation></semantics></math> is
feasible for (P), and</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex33" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{OPT}_{\text{(P)}}=\sum_{l=1}^{L}\alpha_{l}\,e_{l}(r_{l}^{\star})\ \leq\ \sum_{l=1}^{L}\alpha_{l}\,\varepsilon_{l}^{\star}=\mathrm{OPT}_{\text{(E)}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>OPT</mi><mtext>(P)</mtext></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>l</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.611em">≤</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>ε</mi><mi>l</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>OPT</mi><mtext>(E)</mtext></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{OPT}_{\text{(P)}}=\sum_{l=1}^{L}\alpha_{l}\,e_{l}(r_{l}^{\star})\ \leq\ \sum_{l=1}^{L}\alpha_{l}\,\varepsilon_{l}^{\star}=\mathrm{OPT}_{\text{(E)}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">Hence <math id="A2.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{OPT}_{\text{(P)}}\leq\mathrm{OPT}_{\text{(E)}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>OPT</mi><mtext>(P)</mtext></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>OPT</mi><mtext>(E)</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{OPT}_{\text{(P)}}\leq\mathrm{OPT}_{\text{(E)}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Combining both directions yields equality.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Proof of Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma1" title="Lemma 1 (Uniform 𝜀 under homogeneous sensitivity and bounded profiles). ‣ 3.3 Surrogate Pareto Frontier ‣ 3 Pareto-Guided Rank Selection ‣ Activation-Informed Pareto-Guided Low-Rank Compression for Efficient LLM/VLM" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a></h2>

<div id="A3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">Write <math id="A3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{l}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>l</mi></msub><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{l}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{l=1}^{L}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{l=1}^{L}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math>.
By assumption, <math id="A3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{h},\overline{h}:[0,1]\to\mathbb{R}_{\geq 0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder accentunder="true"><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mo>,</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{h},\overline{h}:[0,1]\to\mathbb{R}_{\geq 0}</annotation></semantics></math> are
nonincreasing, convex, and bound each <math id="A3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{l}</annotation></semantics></math> pointwise. The budget range
<math id="A3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L\,\overline{h}(1)\leq b\leq L\,\overline{h}(0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L\,\overline{h}(1)\leq b\leq L\,\overline{h}(0)</annotation></semantics></math> ensures feasibility.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">(i) Symmetric surrogate <math id="A3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{h}</annotation></semantics></math>.</em>
Consider
<math id="A3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\min_{\varepsilon\in[0,1]^{L}}\sum_{l}\varepsilon_{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mmultiscripts><mo>∑</mo><mi>l</mi><mrow></mrow><mprescripts></mprescripts><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>L</mi></msup></mrow><mrow></mrow></mmultiscripts><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\min_{\varepsilon\in[0,1]^{L}}\sum_{l}\varepsilon_{l}</annotation></semantics></math>
s.t. <math id="A3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{l}\overline{h}(\varepsilon_{l})\leq b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>l</mi></msub><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{l}\overline{h}(\varepsilon_{l})\leq b</annotation></semantics></math>.
This program is convex; Slater holds for interior <math id="A3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math>, hence KKT are
necessary and sufficient. Let <math id="A3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> be the multiplier for the
coupling constraint, <math id="A3.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{l},v_{l}\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{l},v_{l}\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A3.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leq\varepsilon_{l}\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leq\varepsilon_{l}\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, and
<math id="A3.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{l}\in\partial\overline{h}(\varepsilon_{l})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">∈</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{l}\in\partial\overline{h}(\varepsilon_{l})</annotation></semantics></math>. KKT:
(i) stationarity <math id="A3.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1+\mu g_{l}-u_{l}+v_{l}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1+\mu g_{l}-u_{l}+v_{l}=0</annotation></semantics></math>,
(ii) complementary slackness <math id="A3.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu\big(\sum_{l}\overline{h}(\varepsilon_{l})-b\big)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em">∑</mo><mi>l</mi></msub><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu\big(\sum_{l}\overline{h}(\varepsilon_{l})-b\big)=0</annotation></semantics></math>,
<math id="A3.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{l}\varepsilon_{l}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{l}\varepsilon_{l}=0</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{l}(\varepsilon_{l}-1)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{l}(\varepsilon_{l}-1)=0</annotation></semantics></math>,
(iii) primal/dual feasibility.
Since <math id="A3.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{h}</annotation></semantics></math> is strictly decreasing and <math id="A3.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math> is nondegenerate,
the coupling constraint is active, so <math id="A3.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.
If <math id="A3.p2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\varepsilon_{l}&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\varepsilon_{l}&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math> then <math id="A3.p2.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{l}=v_{l}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{l}=v_{l}=0</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="A3.p2.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1+\mu g_{l}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1+\mu g_{l}=0</annotation></semantics></math>. Monotonicity of <math id="A3.p2.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial\overline{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial\overline{h}</annotation></semantics></math> (convexity) forces
all interior <math id="A3.p2.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon_{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon_{l}</annotation></semantics></math> to be equal. If some coordinates were at
the boundary while others interior, stationarity with <math id="A3.p2.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and the
monotonicity of <math id="A3.p2.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial\overline{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial\overline{h}</annotation></semantics></math> would conflict with the active
budget unless all <math id="A3.p2.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon_{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon_{l}</annotation></semantics></math> coincide (up to kinks where subgradients
are intervals). Hence there is a uniform optimizer
<math id="A3.p2.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon_{l}\equiv\varepsilon^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>≡</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon_{l}\equiv\varepsilon^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> determined by
<math id="A3.p2.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L\,\overline{h}(\varepsilon^{\star})=b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L\,\overline{h}(\varepsilon^{\star})=b</annotation></semantics></math> (unique on the active segment by
continuity and strict decrease).</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">(ii) Minimax optimality.</em>
Let <math id="A3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}</annotation></semantics></math> be the admissible families with
<math id="A3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{h}\leq h_{l}\leq\overline{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder accentunder="true"><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{h}\leq h_{l}\leq\overline{h}</annotation></semantics></math> pointwise. For any
<math id="A3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{h_{l}\}\in\mathcal{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{h_{l}\}\in\mathcal{H}</annotation></semantics></math> and any <math id="A3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>,
<math id="A3.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{l}h_{l}(\varepsilon_{l})\leq\sum_{l}\overline{h}(\varepsilon_{l})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>l</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≤</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>l</mi></msub><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{l}h_{l}(\varepsilon_{l})\leq\sum_{l}\overline{h}(\varepsilon_{l})</annotation></semantics></math>, hence
<math id="A3.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\varepsilon:\sum_{l}\overline{h}(\varepsilon_{l})\leq b\}\subseteq\{\varepsilon:\sum_{l}h_{l}(\varepsilon_{l})\leq b\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.111em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>l</mi></msub><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.111em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>l</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\varepsilon:\sum_{l}\overline{h}(\varepsilon_{l})\leq b\}\subseteq\{\varepsilon:\sum_{l}h_{l}(\varepsilon_{l})\leq b\}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Minimizing the same linear objective over a smaller set yields a larger
(optimal) value, so the worst case is attained at <math id="A3.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{l}\equiv\overline{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>≡</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{l}\equiv\overline{h}</annotation></semantics></math>.
By (i), its optimizer is uniform. Thus the uniform solution is minimax.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">(iii) Bracketing.</em>
Define <math id="A3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon^{\mathrm{u}},\varepsilon^{\ell}\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>ε</mi><mi>u</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ε</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon^{\mathrm{u}},\varepsilon^{\ell}\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> by
<math id="A3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L\,\overline{h}(\varepsilon^{\mathrm{u}})=b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mi>u</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L\,\overline{h}(\varepsilon^{\mathrm{u}})=b</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="A3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L\,\underline{h}(\varepsilon^{\ell})=b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L\,\underline{h}(\varepsilon^{\ell})=b</annotation></semantics></math>
(use generalized inverses at flats). The uniform vector
<math id="A3.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\varepsilon^{\mathrm{u}},\dots,\varepsilon^{\mathrm{u}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mi>u</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mi>u</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\varepsilon^{\mathrm{u}},\dots,\varepsilon^{\mathrm{u}})</annotation></semantics></math> is feasible
for the true problem since <math id="A3.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{l}\leq\overline{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{l}\leq\overline{h}</annotation></semantics></math>, hence
<math id="A3.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\leq\alpha L\,\varepsilon^{\mathrm{u}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mi>u</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\leq\alpha L\,\varepsilon^{\mathrm{u}}</annotation></semantics></math>. For the lower
bound, replace each <math id="A3.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{l}</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="A3.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder accentunder="true"><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{h}</annotation></semantics></math>, which enlarges the feasible
set; the relaxed problem is convex and, by the same KKT argument, has a
uniform optimum at <math id="A3.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon^{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ε</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon^{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math>, yielding
<math id="A3.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha L\,\varepsilon^{\ell}\leq p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha L\,\varepsilon^{\ell}\leq p</annotation></semantics></math>. Combining gives
<math id="A3.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha L\,\varepsilon^{\ell}\leq p\leq\alpha L\,\varepsilon^{\mathrm{u}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mi>u</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha L\,\varepsilon^{\ell}\leq p\leq\alpha L\,\varepsilon^{\mathrm{u}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Homogeneous Assumption</h2>

<div id="Thmremark1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmremark1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark 1</span></span><span id="Thmremark1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Homogeneous sensitivities as a minimax-robust surrogate)<span id="Thmremark1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmremark1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmremark1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmremark1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Recall problem </span>(E)<span id="Thmremark1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> defined as <math id="Thmremark1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\min_{0\leq\varepsilon_{l}\leq 1}\sum_{l}\alpha_{l}\varepsilon_{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mrow><mmultiscripts><mo>∑</mo><mi>l</mi><mrow></mrow><mprescripts></mprescripts><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow></mrow></mmultiscripts><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\min_{0\leq\varepsilon_{l}\leq 1}\sum_{l}\alpha_{l}\varepsilon_{l}</annotation></semantics></math>
s.t. <math id="Thmremark1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{l}h_{l}(\varepsilon_{l})\leq b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>l</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{l}h_{l}(\varepsilon_{l})\leq b</annotation></semantics></math>.
When <math id="Thmremark1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{l}</annotation></semantics></math> are uncertain, consider the robust counterpart</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex34" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\min_{\varepsilon}\max_{\alpha\in\mathcal{U}}\sum_{l}\alpha_{l}\varepsilon_{l},\quad\mathcal{U}=\{\alpha:\underline{\alpha}_{l}\leq\alpha_{l}\leq\overline{\alpha}_{l}\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mi>ε</mi></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mrow><mmultiscripts><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>l</mi></munder><mprescripts></mprescripts><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi></mrow><mrow></mrow></mmultiscripts><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\min_{\varepsilon}\max_{\alpha\in\mathcal{U}}\sum_{l}\alpha_{l}\varepsilon_{l},\quad\mathcal{U}=\{\alpha:\underline{\alpha}_{l}\leq\alpha_{l}\leq\overline{\alpha}_{l}\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmremark1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmremark1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For any feasible <math id="Thmremark1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>,
<math id="Thmremark1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max_{\alpha\in\mathcal{U}}\sum_{l}\alpha_{l}\varepsilon_{l}=\sum_{l}\overline{\alpha}_{l}\varepsilon_{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mrow><mmultiscripts><mo>∑</mo><mi>l</mi><mrow></mrow><mprescripts></mprescripts><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi></mrow><mrow></mrow></mmultiscripts><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>l</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max_{\alpha\in\mathcal{U}}\sum_{l}\alpha_{l}\varepsilon_{l}=\sum_{l}\overline{\alpha}_{l}\varepsilon_{l}</annotation></semantics></math> since <math id="Thmremark1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon_{l}\!\geq\!0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.108em">≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon_{l}\!\geq\!0</annotation></semantics></math>.
If the bounds are common (<math id="Thmremark1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{\alpha}_{l}=\overline{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{\alpha}_{l}=\overline{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math>), this reduces
exactly to the homogeneous-<math id="Thmremark1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> objective
<math id="Thmremark1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{\alpha}\sum_{l}\varepsilon_{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>l</mi></msub><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{\alpha}\sum_{l}\varepsilon_{l}</annotation></semantics></math>.
If they differ, letting <math id="Thmremark1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\alpha}=\max_{l}\overline{\alpha}_{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\alpha}=\max_{l}\overline{\alpha}_{l}</annotation></semantics></math> gives
<math id="Thmremark1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{l}\overline{\alpha}_{l}\varepsilon_{l}\leq\bar{\alpha}\sum_{l}\varepsilon_{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>l</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>l</mi></msub><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{l}\overline{\alpha}_{l}\varepsilon_{l}\leq\bar{\alpha}\sum_{l}\varepsilon_{l}</annotation></semantics></math>, so minimizing
<math id="Thmremark1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\alpha}\sum_{l}\varepsilon_{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>l</mi></msub><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\alpha}\sum_{l}\varepsilon_{l}</annotation></semantics></math> is <em id="Thmremark1.p1.2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_upright">minimax-safe</em>.
Thus, <math id="Thmremark1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{l}\equiv\bar{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>≡</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{l}\equiv\bar{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> provides a principled robust surrogate for </span>(E)<span id="Thmremark1.p1.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 2 (Uniform 𝜀 yields the surrogate Pareto front of (B)). ‣ 3.3 Surrogate Pareto Frontier ‣ 3 Pareto-Guided Rank Selection ‣ Activation-Informed Pareto-Guided Low-Rank Compression for Efficient LLM/VLM" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a></h2>

<div id="A5.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">Fix a uniform tolerance <math id="A5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> and let
<math id="A5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{l}(\varepsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{l}(\varepsilon)</annotation></semantics></math> be the minimal SVD rank per layer achieving
<math id="A5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{l}\!\big(r_{l}(\varepsilon)\big)\leq\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{l}\!\big(r_{l}(\varepsilon)\big)\leq\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math> (by EYM).
Set</span></p>
<table id="A5.EGx20" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex35"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle H(\varepsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle H(\varepsilon)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex35.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle:=\sum_{l=1}^{L}P_{l}\!\big(r_{l}(\varepsilon)\big)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle:=\sum_{l=1}^{L}P_{l}\!\big(r_{l}(\varepsilon)\big),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex36"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle A(\varepsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle A(\varepsilon)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex36.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle:=\sum_{l=1}^{L}\alpha_{l}\,e_{l}\!\big(r_{l}(\varepsilon)\big)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle:=\sum_{l=1}^{L}\alpha_{l}\,e_{l}\!\big(r_{l}(\varepsilon)\big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A5.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">By the Rank–<math id="A5.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math> Allocation Equivalence (Prop. <a href="#Thmproposition1" title="Proposition 1 (Rank–𝜀 Allocation Equivalence). ‣ 3.3 Surrogate Pareto Frontier ‣ 3 Pareto-Guided Rank Selection ‣ Activation-Informed Pareto-Guided Low-Rank Compression for Efficient LLM/VLM" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>),
the constrained surrogate problem “minimize <math id="A5.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{l}\alpha_{l}e_{l}(r_{l})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>l</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{l}\alpha_{l}e_{l}(r_{l})</annotation></semantics></math>
subject to <math id="A5.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{l}P_{l}(r_{l})\leq b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>l</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{l}P_{l}(r_{l})\leq b</annotation></semantics></math>” is equivalent to its <math id="A5.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-formulation.
Under the homogeneous sensitivity and bounded-profile assumption
(Theorem <a href="#Thmlemma1" title="Lemma 1 (Uniform 𝜀 under homogeneous sensitivity and bounded profiles). ‣ 3.3 Surrogate Pareto Frontier ‣ 3 Pareto-Guided Rank Selection ‣ Activation-Informed Pareto-Guided Low-Rank Compression for Efficient LLM/VLM" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>), the optimal solution of this surrogate
for any budget <math id="A5.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math> is attained by a <em id="A5.p2.1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">uniform</em> tolerance across layers.
Choosing <math id="A5.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b:=H(\varepsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b:=H(\varepsilon)</annotation></semantics></math>, the uniform choice at level <math id="A5.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>
is therefore optimal among all feasible allocations with total parameters
<math id="A5.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\leq H(\varepsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\leq H(\varepsilon)</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e., there is no other feasible allocation that
simultaneously achieves <math id="A5.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{l}P_{l}(r_{l})\leq H(\varepsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>l</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{l}P_{l}(r_{l})\leq H(\varepsilon)</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="A5.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{l}\alpha_{l}e_{l}(r_{l})&lt;A(\varepsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>l</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{l}\alpha_{l}e_{l}(r_{l})&lt;A(\varepsilon)</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence
<math id="A5.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\big(H(\varepsilon),A(\varepsilon)\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\big(H(\varepsilon),A(\varepsilon)\big)</annotation></semantics></math> is (surrogate) Pareto-optimal for (B).</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A5.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">If <math id="A5.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon,\varepsilon^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon,\varepsilon^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> induce the same rank vector
<math id="A5.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\big(r_{l}(\varepsilon)\big)_{l}=\big(r_{l}(\varepsilon^{\prime})\big)_{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\big(r_{l}(\varepsilon)\big)_{l}=\big(r_{l}(\varepsilon^{\prime})\big)_{l}</annotation></semantics></math>, then
<math id="A5.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(\varepsilon)=H(\varepsilon^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(\varepsilon)=H(\varepsilon^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="A5.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A(\varepsilon)=A(\varepsilon^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A(\varepsilon)=A(\varepsilon^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> by definition, so they correspond to the same
frontier point.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix F </span>Derivation of ALS Updates</h2>

<div id="A6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We minimize</p>
<table id="A6.EGx21" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.E7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\min_{\mathbf{A},\mathbf{B}}\;\;\|\mathbf{W}\mathbf{X}-\mathbf{A}\mathbf{B}\mathbf{X}\|_{F}^{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐁</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.560em">⁡</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝐖𝐗</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐀𝐁𝐗</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\min_{\mathbf{A},\mathbf{B}}\;\;\|\mathbf{W}\mathbf{X}-\mathbf{A}\mathbf{B}\mathbf{X}\|_{F}^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{M}=\mathbf{X}\mathbf{X}^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐌</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>𝐗𝐗</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{M}=\mathbf{X}\mathbf{X}^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math> and using the Frobenius identity
<math id="A6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\mathbf{Y}\|_{F}^{2}=\mathrm{tr}(\mathbf{Y}\mathbf{Y}^{\top})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝐘</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐘𝐘</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\mathbf{Y}\|_{F}^{2}=\mathrm{tr}(\mathbf{Y}\mathbf{Y}^{\top})</annotation></semantics></math>, we write</p>
<table id="A6.EGx22" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex37"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{tr}\!\left((\mathbf{W}-\mathbf{A}\mathbf{B})\mathbf{M}(\mathbf{W}-\mathbf{A}\mathbf{B})^{\top}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.670em;" width="0.670em"><mi>tr</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐖</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐀𝐁</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐌</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐖</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐀𝐁</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{tr}\!\left((\mathbf{W}-\mathbf{A}\mathbf{B})\mathbf{M}(\mathbf{W}-\mathbf{A}\mathbf{B})^{\top}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.Ex38"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathrm{tr}(\mathbf{W}\mathbf{M}\mathbf{W}^{\top})-2\,\mathrm{tr}(\mathbf{A}\mathbf{B}\mathbf{M}\mathbf{W}^{\top})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐖𝐌𝐖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>tr</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐀𝐁𝐌𝐖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathrm{tr}(\mathbf{W}\mathbf{M}\mathbf{W}^{\top})-2\,\mathrm{tr}(\mathbf{A}\mathbf{B}\mathbf{M}\mathbf{W}^{\top})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
